.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt OXDOC 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm oxdoc
.Nd format and check manual pages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl T Ar device
.Op Fl O Ar option Ns Op , Ns Ar option ...
.Op Fl W Ar level
.Op Ar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility formats manual pages written in the
.Xr mdoc 7
language, and in the
.Xr roff 7
requests and escapes that pages use.
It reads each
.Ar file ,
or the standard input if none is given, and writes the formatted page to
the standard output.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl O Ar option
Set output options, separated by commas:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm width Ns = Ns Ar columns
The line length.
The default is the terminal's width, at most 80, less two; or 78 when the
output is not a terminal.
.It Cm overstrike
Show bold and underline as backspace overstrike
.Pq Ql c\eb\&c , Ql _\eb\&c
rather than as terminal escape sequences, for pagers and
.Xr col 1 .
.It Cm plain
No bold or underline at all.
.It Cm os Ns = Ns Ar name
The operating system name for a page whose
.Ic \&Os
macro has no argument.
.El
.It Fl T Ar device
The output device:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm utf8
Terminal text in UTF-8, the default when the locale names UTF-8.
.It Cm ascii
Terminal text in ASCII, the default otherwise.
.It Cm lint
No output; report every diagnostic, including style suggestions.
.It Cm tree
The parsed document tree, for debugging.
.El
.It Fl W Ar level
Report diagnostics at
.Ar level
and above:
.Cm style ,
.Cm warning
(the default),
.Cm error
or
.Cm unsupp .
.Cm all
is
.Cm style ;
.Cm stop
stops after the first file with a diagnostic at the chosen level.
.El
.Pp
Bold and underline are shown when the output is a terminal, as SGR escape
sequences, and not otherwise.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LC_ALL , LC_CTYPE , LANG
The first of these that is set decides the default device:
.Cm utf8
if it names UTF-8,
.Cm ascii
otherwise.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
No diagnostic at
.Cm warning
level or above.
.It 1
At least one such diagnostic.
.It 2
A usage error, or a file could not be read.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics have the form
.Dl oxdoc: Ar file : Ns Ar line : Ns Ar column : Ar LEVEL : Ar message : Ar detail
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr more 1 ,
.Xr man 7 ,
.Xr mdoc 7 ,
.Xr roff 7 ,
.Xr tbl 7
.Sh STANDARDS
The output follows the formatting of
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
which the other BSDs use.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility was written for OxideBSD.
.Sh BUGS
The
.Xr eqn 7
preprocessor is not implemented yet; neither are the HTML and Markdown
devices.
